  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scaling up successful project that Develops Libraries and Reading Centres to Rur</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Recent tests of primary school children in Ethiopia have revealed high levels of illiteracy and very poor reading ability among primary children in rural schools. This project will scale up the successful work of a pilot intervention which improved students&apos; access to books and other reading matter through libraries, teacher training and the production of low cost sets of books for teacher and class use. The books contain teaching on disability and health care, and are produced by disabled people in a linked association. The whole project will cover seventy five schools over three years, and will be mirrored by a spin-off one run by Link Ethiopia, following the same resources and pattern.</narrative>
  </description>
